{% comment %}
  Product recommendations (spec 09): "Vous aimerez aussi".

  Server-rendered from the Product Recommendations API. When that has run, the
  products are already in the HTML — the page is complete before any JavaScript
  executes, which matters on a phone on a Moroccan mobile connection.

  product-recommendations.js then re-fetches this same section through the
  Section Rendering API the first time the block approaches the viewport, so the
  row fills in on a product that was created after the page was cached, and
  nothing is requested for a recommendation the shopper never scrolls to.

  When the API has not run — the state the store is in today, with no catalogue —
  the block falls back to four products from the product's first collection,
  minus the product itself. With neither, the heading and the row are not
  rendered at all: an empty "Vous aimerez aussi" is worse than no section, and
  the fetch above can still fill the block in.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign rec_limit = 4
  assign fallback_collection = product.collections.first

  # Liquid has no way to build an array of objects, so the fallback is counted
  # here and drawn below with the same two rules: skip the product itself, stop
  # at four.
  assign fallback_count = 0
  if fallback_collection != blank
    for candidate in fallback_collection.products limit: 8
      if candidate.id != product.id
        assign fallback_count = fallback_count | plus: 1
        if fallback_count == rec_limit
          break
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  <div
    class="product-recommendations"
    data-recommendations
    data-recommendations-url="{{ routes.product_recommendations_url }}?section_id={{ section.id }}&product_id={{ product.id }}&limit={{ rec_limit }}&intent=related"
  >
    {%- if recommendations.performed? and recommendations.products_count > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Server-rendered from the Product Recommendations API: the row is complete
        in the first paint, before any JavaScript runs and on a phone that
        cannot afford a second round trip.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="recommendations">
        <h2 class="recommendations__title t-display">
          {{- 'rifano.product_you_may_also_like' | t -}}
        </h2>
        <ul class="recommendations__track" data-recommendations-track tabindex="0">
          {%- for item in recommendations.products limit: rec_limit -%}
            <li class="recommendations__item">
              {% render 'product-card', product: item, sizes: '(min-width: 1200px) 20vw, (min-width: 768px) 28vw, 44vw' %}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- elsif fallback_count > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The API had nothing. Four products from the product's first collection,
        minus the product itself, so the shelf is never a mirror of the product
        the shopper is already looking at.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="recommendations">
        <h2 class="recommendations__title t-display">
          {{- 'rifano.product_you_may_also_like' | t -}}
        </h2>
        <ul class="recommendations__track" data-recommendations-track tabindex="0">
          {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
          {%- for candidate in fallback_collection.products limit: 8 -%}
            {%- if candidate.id != product.id -%}
              {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
              <li class="recommendations__item">
                {% render 'product-card', product: candidate, sizes: '(min-width: 1200px) 20vw, (min-width: 768px) 28vw, 44vw' %}
              </li>
              {%- if shown == rec_limit -%}
                {%- break -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<script src="{{ 'product-recommendations.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product recommendations",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Product recommendations" }]
}
{% endschema %}